        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0268" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg174"/>

                <head>No. 136.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 11, 1886</date>.
                        (Received January 21, 1887.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 263.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    consul-general has submitted to me the following question: “Is the storage of
                    opium by an American firm forbidden under Article II of the treaty of 1880?”</p>
                <pb facs="0269" n="175" xml:id="pg175"/>
                <p>I have declined to answer this question specifically, but I have held that, under
                    the facts communicated to me, Messrs. Russell &amp; Co. were acting contrary to
                    the treaty.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith a copy of my answer, which I submit to you for approval.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d136-a1.xml" xpointer="d136-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
